# Machine-local registry pins written by `npm-pin` and the post-checkout hook in
# templates/git-template. These carry a private registry hostname on work
# machines and are per-checkout, so they must never be committed anywhere.
# Ignoring them here keeps `git status` clean in every repo without editing each
# repo's .git/info/exclude. A repo that legitimately tracks its own .npmrc is
# unaffected: gitignore never applies to files already in the index. To add one
# deliberately, use `git add -f .npmrc`.
.npmrc
